#### Current Updated Meeting Notes by line Manager

**Graeme Wright 1:1 Meetings** 

**Key roles and responsibilities:** 

- Digital TLA Strategies targeted for specific staff members in Sixth Form 

- Effective use of immersive reader 

- A project to look at how parent reports for sixth form can be pulled through into one report. Emily said Linda Perry has used something for EMT in the past so may be a good contact to discuss with.  

- Video tools for teams environment locally – accessibility guides need to be professionally created (longer!)  

- Shadow TLAM and TLAC Activities over next couple of weeks 

- Digital champion reframing – who will provide GW with the digital intelligence to review their fundamentals 

- **Modelling**  

- Staff can use digital inking within a Microsoft Whiteboard or PowerPoint slide - both pre-shared on Teams 

- Screen Recording in PowerPoint to capture those moments of demonstrations and modelling 

- Screen Recorders using visualisers 

- WHY - this will allow those catching up, revision, support etc 

- WHY - this supports feedback loop and curious pedagogical tla discussion s with learners 

- **Feedback Loop:** 

- In addition to in class questioning, cold calling, 1:1 or group work... 

- Plickers - a non-tech digital resource that allows teachers to ask multiple choice questions, gather the responses of every learner, and track progress over time. Students do not need digital resources, just a reusable QR code type resource. Tutors do need a phone or a resource that has a camera to capture responses. Completely GDPR compliant if set up properly. 

- Forms Quizzes - Set up with auto marking and auto feedback. learners may need teaching about how to access it, but they are a click away from feedback. Branching can be set up to include support for learners who are stuck or need more help on an answer. Can embed all types of resources - Eg, docs, videos, links 

- WHY - Great tool for Starter / Warm Up / Review activities – E.g. working on a 5 questions example. 2 from last week, 2 from last lesson, 1 from last month or unit /topic 

- WHY - learners get immediate feedback on their performance. Tutors get data to inform their planning. Massively saves time from marking loads, to redirect into planning and impact time. 

- **Questioning ****&**** AI:** 

- AI to help devise questions following progress data analysis 

- AI to help develop strategies for differentiation and student groups based on needs and knowledge gaps 

- AI Agents for marking 

- **Digital pedagogies:** 

- Foundations of best digital practice – accessibility and inclusive nature of resources (teams, resources, tracking and monitoring, purpose and IMAPCT, informed TLA practice based on intent, purpose and intended outcome, time efficient use of Digital tools to improve TLA Practice 

- **21****st**** Century design practice** 

- Autonomy and learner informed practice  

- How do you learn / creating autonomous and independent learners 

 

**Core Priorities:** 

- Teams environments (Teams health check) – accessible, inclusive with a solid foundation – teams health check; Accessibility toolkit (staff and learner focused) 

Teams checks lists; Video guides for key priorities; Identified Digital leads (digital champions) and train the trainer approach 

- E.g. immersive reader; teams channels and files (what is coming next) 

- Engagement strategies – open channels Q&A / sharing / well-being 

- Assessment tracking and monitoring – summative and formative feedback 

- Use of AI for impactful strategies and time efficiencies – Power Automate 

- Joe Abdulgani – coaching on Co-Pilot options (all levels of the organisations)  

- Training and coaching at all levels across the organisation 

- Modelling – all the above and links / application to TLA strategies 

