### Exploring EIF Toolkit and College Response

1) Initial Assessment and Starting Points - Inspectors expect providers to know learners’ starting points in English, maths and digital skills. 

EVIDENCE: Digital skills baseline assessment

QUESTION: 

How do we know? 

How is this assessed? 

What are Digital Skills, specifically the defined difference between IT Skills and Digital Skills?

Is there a current list of General Digital Skills on record at WC?

2) Digital Skills Development - Evidence:

•	Use of digital learning platforms

•	Coursework requiring digital research

•	Use of spreadsheets, presentations or specialist software

•	Digital portfolio submissions

•	Online collaboration tools

•	Training on workplace technology

QUESTION: 

How is this done - we say it is, how is this currently measured.

What does this mean specifically? - "Inspectors will look for purposeful use, not just basic IT access."

Do these exist? - "Schemes of work integrating English, maths and digital skills"

Who is currently delivering this? - "Digital skills workshops"

What do learners already say about Digital Skills?

